hermes v0.23.0: a background delegate_task the full async pool refuses
is rejected right away instead of running inline.

Root cause. tools/delegate_tool_dispatch.py _dispatch_background: when the
first unit of a background call was refused by the async registry
(tools/async_delegation.py _dispatch_admitted, "Async delegation capacity
reached (N running)"), it ran the whole batch synchronously
(_run_sync_with_note(batch, "at_capacity")) inside the parent's tool call.
The parent's turn then blocked for the child's whole run: new user
messages, steers and finished background results queued behind it, and
slots freed meanwhile made no difference. The model learned why only from
a note on the result, after the inline run.

Fix:
- _dispatch_admitted tags the capacity refusal with reason "at_capacity"
  (the same marker the upstream fix uses).
- _dispatch_background returns {"status": "rejected", "error":
  "background delegation pool full (N/N running); nothing was started.
  ..."} at once (the upstream fix's wording): children are released (_release_unstarted_child after
  _restore_parent_cancellation), their live transcripts and manifest are
  settled as rejected and the call's metrics row is closed. No slot, no
  attached child, no running transcript is left behind.
- Other refusals of the first unit (backend retiring, session closed,
  scheduler failure) still run inline as before, as does a later unit
  of an admitted call (it shares the call's slot, so it is never refused
  for capacity: only scheduler failures reach that path).
- The restart re-dispatch (hermes-subagents-resume-after-restart.patch,
  _RESUME_META) is unchanged: it still gets "re-dispatch cannot run
  inline (at_capacity)", which session_auto_continue matches to park the
  unit until a slot frees.
- Sessions that cannot receive detached results ("no_async": hermes -z,
  cron, ...) still run inline.

Test: tests/tools/test_delegate_capacity_interrupt.py
test_full_pool_rejects_without_running_inline (cap 1: the second call is
rejected within 1 s, its child never starts and is closed, the slot count
stays 1 and the freed slot admits the next call); its parametrized test
drops the "capacity" case, which no longer runs inline. Fails without
the fix (the second call ran inline for 30 s), passes with it; upstream's
own repro test (tests/tools/test_delegate_capacity_rejection.py of the
upstream PR, fix commit d5522f1f2d) passes against this tree as well.
Differences from that fix: it renames the remaining inline note to
"not_accepted", which here would break the resume patch's "at_capacity"
match, so the key stays; this patch also closes the call's metrics row.

Generated against v0.23.0 with every earlier patch of
modules/core/package.nix applied.

